Subject: [PATCH 02340/11362] [outer-loop] engine A/B: v2-BFS dominant; v3
 cracks no deep game (engine choice ruled out)

Operator: 'build the engine A/B.' Ran v2-BFS vs v3-novelty vs v3+learned-verifier
over 3 solved + 3 deep games (reproduction-gated, results/arc_engine_ab.json):

 SOLVED: v2-BFS wins all on path-optimality -- su15 7/1746, r11l 3/2236, cd82 5/525.
   v3-novelty solves them too but with 4-15x LONGER paths (29/58/15 acts) -- best-
   first-by-novelty doesn't minimize path length, bad for action-scored ARC.
 DEEP: wa30/g50t/sb26 fail under BOTH engines at 20k -- a generic engine swap is NOT
   the deep-tail lever.
 SIGNAL: a learned verifier guiding v3 cut r11l expansions -52% (1064 vs 2236) but
   lost path-optimality (6 vs 3 acts) -> the efficiency lever is a GOOD per-game
   verifier (= the OfflineSolver/verifier-routed path that already works for lp85),
   NOT a generic novelty engine.

CONCLUSION: engine routing collapses to 'v2-BFS for first-contact'; no separate
engine-selector needed. The deep tail needs per-game RE + a trained per-game
verifier/representation (GAP-ARC-TRM-TRAINED-ON-ARC), not engine choice.
GAP-ARC-ROUTER-ENGINE-LABELS answered. (v3 stats param committed separately.)
